cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "untell — an AI-detector auditing toolkit"
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it."
type: software
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-08-09"
authors:
  - name: "untell contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ssamba1/untell"
url: "https://github.com/ssamba1/untell"
abstract: >-
  An open-source AI-detector auditing toolkit that measures detector false-positive rates on human
  writing and verdict stability, using a detector-in-the-loop harness that rewrites text against a multi-detector
  ensemble (local proxy detectors plus key-gated commercial APIs) using each detector's score as feedback,
  gated on a semantic-similarity meaning-preservation constraint and byte-for-byte preservation of citations,
  numbers, quotes, and named entities. Packaged as a Claude Code skill and a Python CLI. Research and
  defensive tool.
keywords:
  - detector-evaluation
  - ai-detection
  - detector-feedback
  - false-positives
  - nlp
  - claude-skill
license: MIT
